ralph/progress.txt:33371:- Repository CRUD-and-invariants for a TABLE WHOSE MIGRATION + REPOSITORY DO NOT EXIST YET, WITH A NARROW APPEND + READ + ONE-MUTATION (RESOLVE) LIFECYCLE AND OPTIONAL POLYMORPHIC NULLABLE RESOURCE LEGS PINNED BY MATCH-SIMPLE COMPOSITE FKs (BE-0471 pattern, internal/controlplane/store/drift_finding.go + drift_finding_repository_invariants_test.go + migrate/migrations/0037_drift_findings.{up,down}.sql). Subspecies of the BE-0463 (job_attempts) new-table template with five load-bearing deltas: (a) the lifecycle has TWO writes (Append + MarkResolved) rather than one (Append) and NO append-only trigger — the resolved_at + resolved_by_actor_id transition is a legal UPDATE, paired by a drift_findings_resolved_consistent CHECK that ties the two columns nil-state-together. The migration uses set_updated_at trigger (not bump_version + version column) because there is no measurable optimistic-concurrency contention on operator-driven resolution; the file header documents the version-column-omission as load-bearing so a future bulk-resolve story knows it must add a new migration + version column rather than retrofit one. (b) The optional resource legs are NULLABLE composite FKs on (organization_id, project_id|environment_id|service_id|service_domain_id) referencing the parents' UNIQUE (organization_id, id) — MATCH SIMPLE so the FK fires only when the column is set. The repository serialises a blank Go string to SQL NULL via a private nullIfEmpty(s string) any helper (so a `f.ProjectID = ""` Append lands as project_id IS NULL on disk, and the composite FK does not engage with a non-existent empty-string id). scanDriftFinding reads *string into scratch and projects nil onto "" so the public DriftFinding struct collapses NULL onto the zero value (matching JobAttempt / DeploymentEvent — the customer never observes the distinction). Forward-applicable to any future polymorphic-resource-leg table (a future cost_attributions_findings or capacity_breaches tabl